# Ad spend sync.
#
# With these unset the app still works: ad spend is entered by hand from
# Business -> Money -> Marketing -> Log ad spend, which is the intended fallback.
#
# To pull it from Meta automatically:
#   1. business.facebook.com -> Business settings -> Users -> System users
#   2. Add a system user and give it the ad account with "View performance"
#   3. Generate a token with the `ads_read` scope. System user tokens do not
#      expire; the ordinary user tokens last 60 days and will stop working.
#   4. The ad account id is the number after `act_` in the Ads Manager URL.
#
# Then restart the server. It pulls at boot and once a day after that, always
# re-reading the last 14 days because Meta restates recent figures.

# META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Stripe payments and their exact fees.
#
# Use a RESTRICTED key, not the full secret key.
#
# Stripe dashboard -> Developers -> API keys -> Create restricted key
#   "How will you be using this key?"  ->  Powering an integration you built
#
# Then set these five to Read, and leave everything else on None:
#   Charges             (Core)
#   Balance transactions / Balance transaction sources  (Core)
#   PaymentIntents      (Core)
#   Customers           (Core)
#   Invoices            (Billing)
#
# That is everything this needs, and a read-only key cannot move money.
#
# Check it with:  npm run test:stripe --prefix server

# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_live_...
